{
 "title": "A guarded dependency call and circuit breaker states",
 "description": "The caller sends requests through a bounded client that applies a deadline, a bulkhead pool and a circuit breaker before calling the dependency. The breaker moves from closed to open when failures cross a threshold, from open to half-open when a wait elapses, from half-open to closed when trial calls succeed, and back to open when a trial call fails.",
